 - Big screen avoids duplicate visible text (title only in the lobby h1, join link only once per view) so text-based
   locators stay unique.
 
+## Prizes (scoring, leaderboard, winners)
+- Schema step 3: `quizzes.winners` ("Number of winners", integer ≥ 1, default 3; on both quiz forms, validated
+  server-side, 422 on error) and `game_winners (game_id, player_id)`. Export/import don't carry `winners` (the format
+  stays exactly as documented); an imported quiz gets the default 3.
+- Score (`db::leaderboard`): 1 point per correct answer. Ties are broken by the total time of the correct answers, where
+  time = `answers.answered_at` (server time of the last accepted pick) − `game_questions.opened_at`. Then join order,
+  so the order is total and the place = index + 1 (no shared places). Every player of the game is listed, 0 points included.
+- Points are shown only after "End quiz" (phone: "Place X of Y", "N points"/"1 point"; big screen: `ol.leaderboard > li.leader`
+  with place, name, points, and a `leader__badge` "Winner"). The time is only in the `title` tooltip.
+- Over-phase controls: "Top N" (`POST …/top`), "Draw" (`…/draw`), "Reset winners" (`…/reset-winners`). N is read from the
+  quiz at click time. These are not `seq`-guarded (each Draw click draws again) and only work once the game is over.
+  `db::set_winners` replaces the set and bumps `games.seq` + `hub.bump_phase()`, so the screen and phones re-render live.
+- Rules (`prizes.rs`): 0 points never wins; if ≤ N players have points, all of them win. Draw: players with more points
+  than the N-th place win, the rest is drawn (uniform, `/dev/urandom`) among exactly the N-th place's points (speed ignored).
+- Latency: phase changes are pushed immediately. The big-screen stream coalesces only stats bursts (100ms), and a phase
+  change cuts that pause short. (Before, every event waited 100ms.)
+
